  "article_notes": "Experimental B. rossi infection in 5 purpose-bred castrated male Beagles: 3 high-dose (HD, 10^8 parasites) and 2 low-dose (LD, 10^4). The dose groups are the only severity contrast: all HD dogs collapsed (habitus 1+) and were treated at 96 h; no LD dog collapsed or reached an end point (LD treated at 108 h). Groups are therefore defined by inoculum dose, coinciding with collapse; treated as a severity definition (outcome_class other). HD vs LD compared at each timepoint with linear mixed models (Bonferroni). Values are median (range). Samples before treatment up to 96 h (HD) / 108 h (LD), after treatment thereafter, so sample_timing is mixed. Significance for non-listed timepoints is inferred from the text, which names only the significant timepoints (the figures mark significant timepoints with bars, not readable in the text). Same dogs as Smith et al. 2021 and Atkinson et al. 2022 (transcriptomic/cytokine reports of the same experimental infection). Comparisons with pre-infection baseline (within-group changes over time) not extracted. Cortisol-T4-TSH correlations are between markers, not with severity.",
